{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1776870222,"nonce":"SK2gcyOciPDZXssbA5svZnA5bDo=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABAORxLQ","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/78","origin":"github"},"title":"H.265 transport rollout on izzyboat / bizzyboat (launch + udp_bridge)","message":"## Background\n\nFollow-up to [unh_marine_perception#4](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_perception/issues/4) (on-device H.265 in `depthai_marine`). That issue splits into a code-only change in `unh_marine_perception` and a platform-side rollout here. This issue tracks the platform-side work for izzyboat/bizzyboat: launch and `udp_bridge` config to actually use the new H.265 streams over LTE / Starlink.\n\n## Split by camera type\n\nInvestigation on `depthai_ros_driver` (jazzy, v2.12.2) confirmed:\n\n- **Plain-streaming / detection cameras (already on `depthai_ros_driver`)**: H.265 is available via YAML params — no C++ change required.\n  - `rgb.i_low_bandwidth: true`\n  - `rgb.i_low_bandwidth_profile: H265_MAIN` (also `H264_MAIN`, `MJPEG`)\n  - `rgb.i_low_bandwidth_bitrate: \u003ckbps\u003e`\n  - `rgb.i_low_bandwidth_frame_freq: \u003cframes\u003e` (keyframe cadence)\n  - The driver publishes `FFMPEGPacket` via `ffmpeg_image_transport` on `image_raw` (no `/compressed` suffix; the transport plugin picks it up by topic).\n  - izzyboat's `forward_oak` (driven by `izzyboat_project11/config/jolo_hd.yaml`) falls in this bucket.\n\n- **Segmentation cameras (running `sea_surface_segmentation`)**: H.265 requires `unh_marine_perception#4` to land. The driver's `Segmentation` NN family hardcodes DeepLab argmax decoding, incompatible with the custom 3-class softmax-as-RGB output the downstream `sea_surface_layer` / `segments_to_pointcloud` consume. Changing that contract is out of scope; this issue assumes the `depthai_marine` H.265 branch from #4 is used for these cameras.\n\n## Scope\n\n### In scope\n\n- **izzyboat forward_oak (driver-side)**: update `izzyboat_project11/config/jolo_hd.yaml` to enable H.265 low-bandwidth streaming. Tune `i_low_bandwidth_bitrate` to match the [#4 calibration](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_perception/issues/4) findings.\n- **izzyboat / bizzyboat segmentation cameras (depthai_marine-side)**: once #4 ships, enable the new `h265_enable` / `h265_bitrate_kbps` / `h265_keyframe_frequency_frames` / `h265_profile` params in the platform launch files that spawn `sea_surface_segmentation`.\n- **udp_bridge config**: add the new `\u003ccamera\u003e/image_raw/ffmpeg` (FFMPEGPacket) topics to the OTH subscriber list and remove or de-prioritize the JPEG topics they replace. Keep JPEG during rollout per #4's strategy.\n- **Rollout plan**: one platform first (izzyboat preferred per #4), validate on the water, then repeat for bizzyboat.\n\n### Out of scope\n\n- Adaptive bitrate by link (LTE vs. Starlink). Follow-up after the static numbers are known.\n- Removing JPEG paths entirely. Keep as fallback during rollout.\n- Any operator-station decoder changes beyond confirming `ffmpeg_image_transport` picks up the streams. Bag recording / dashboard updates tracked separately if needed.\n\n## Pre-requisites\n\n- Physical OAK access on the target platform (blocker, same as #4).\n- [#4](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_perception/issues/4) merged, or at least its code-only sub-PR merged.\n- Calibration numbers from #4 to inform initial bitrate defaults.\n\n## Downstream consumers to enumerate\n\nBefore the cutover, confirm these are ready:\n\n- `udp_bridge` config (this repo).\n- Operator-station bag recording — topic list needs the `/ffmpeg` siblings.\n- Any dashboard / camp UI that subscribes to per-camera image topics.\n- Any throttle / republish nodes in platform launch files (jolo_launch.py has two `throttle` nodes on `/compressed` — if we cut over to FFMPEGPacket, these either follow or get replaced).\n\n## Deliverables\n\n- PRs updating `izzyboat_project11/config/jolo_hd.yaml` and any bizzyboat equivalents.\n- PRs updating `udp_bridge` subscriber lists.\n- Short writeup (this repo's deployment log or `docs/`) comparing pre-cutover vs. post-cutover LTE / Starlink bandwidth on a representative run.\n- Follow-up issue if adaptive-bitrate work is warranted.\n\n## Related\n\n- [unh_marine_perception#4](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_perception/issues/4) — depthai_marine on-device H.265 encoding\n- [unh_marine_perception#2](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_perception/issues/2) / PR #3 — software benchmark baseline\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}